      "artist": "HARTLEPOOLMARINA2014",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Scone Palace Memorial within the Moot Hill Chapel",
      "description": "Memorial of Countess Henrietta Frederica von Bünau (Lady Stormont, d.1766), daughter of German-Saxon Count Heinrich von Bünau. contained her heart and presumably her husband (David Murray, 7th Viscount Stormont, 2nd Earl of Mansfield, d.1796)'s heart too. Photo by Michael Garlick.\nThe Latin Inscriptions :\n\"The husband wished that what remains of her beloved heart be placed in this urn\" AD 1766.\n\"Remembering each other's love forever and now, at last, he adds his own\" AD 1796\n\n\"Dedicated to Henrietta Frederica Stormont, daughter of the Count of Bunau, wife of David, Viscount of Stormont, ambassador of Great Britain to the Holy Roman Empire. Flourishing in the prime of life, in talent, in beauty, remarkable for every praise, endowed with every virtue, she met a death happy to herself, [but] deeply bitter to her friends, parents and most wretched husband. March 16, 1766.\"",
      "dateCreated": "2013-06-29 12:05:58",
